      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_cbecb360",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a smiling emoji with rainbow stripes (symbolizing LGBTQ+ identity) and glasses, overlaid with the text 'when you're the gay friend and also the meme lord.' The scene is lighthearted and self-deprecating, celebrating a person who identifies as gay and is also known for creating or popularizing memes. There is no toxicity present in this meme. It does not contain abusive, cyberbullying, harmful, hateful, misogynous, or propaganda elements. The intent is to humorously acknowledge and celebrate the dual identity of being both a gay friend and a meme creator, using the rainbow emoji as a visual metaphor for LGBTQ+ pride and the glasses as a common meme trope for 'nerd' or 'smart' personas. The overall intent is self-referential and celebratory, not targeting or disparaging any group.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_02d34e9e"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
